---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const link =
  "text-umber-700 underline decoration-umber-500/50 underline-offset-2";
---
<Base
  title="Leaves.PH · does less canopy mean more flooding?"
  pathname="/flood-risk"
  description="Testing the link between tree canopy and flooding across Metro Manila barangays, using observed July 2025 radar inundation and a confounder-controlled model. A co-occurrence screen, not a causal claim."
>
  <div id="fl-root" data-lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 pt-12 pb-16 text-ink-700 leading-[1.7]">

    <!-- ── header + language toggle ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
      <p class="kicker">METHOD &middot; FLOODING AND THE CANOPY</p>
      <div class="shrink-0 inline-flex border border-ink-900 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.12em]" role="group" aria-label="Language">
        <button id="lang-en" type="button" class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-forest-700 text-paper" aria-pressed="true">EN</button>
        <button id="lang-tl" type="button" class="px-2.5 py-1 bg-paper text-ink-700" aria-pressed="false">TL</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h1 data-en class="font-display font-medium tracking-tight text-ink-900 mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.05;">Does losing trees flood a barangay?</h1>
    <h1 data-tl class="font-display font-medium tracking-tight text-ink-900 mb-3" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem); line-height: 1.05;">Bumabaha ba ang barangay dahil sa nawalang puno?</h1>

    <p data-en class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-6 max-w-narrow">
      A fair question, and a tempting story: less canopy, more runoff, more flooding. So we tested it. We laid the
      <a href="/" class={link}>per-barangay canopy</a> series next to how much of each Metro Manila barangay the radar
      actually saw under water in the July 2025 monsoon flood, and asked what really predicts where it flooded. The
      answer is honest and a little against the grain.
    </p>
    <p data-tl class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-6 max-w-narrow">
      Patas na tanong, at kaakit-akit na kuwento: kaunting puno, mas maraming tubig, mas maraming baha. Kaya sinubok
      namin. Pinagtabi namin ang <a href="/" class={link}>canopy kada barangay</a> at kung gaano kalaki ng bawat
      barangay sa Metro Manila ang nakitang lubog ng radar noong baha ng Hulyo 2025, at tinanong kung ano talaga ang
      humuhula kung saan bumaha. Tapat ang sagot, at bahagyang salungat sa inaasahan.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── headline finding (filled from the summary JSON) ──────────────── -->
    <div class="border border-ink-900 bg-paper-tint/40 p-5 sm:p-6">
      <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-en>WHAT THE DATA SHOWS</p>
      <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-tl>ANG IPINAPAKITA NG DATOS</p>
      <p class="stat-medium" id="hl-verdict">&mdash;</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 mt-2 leading-relaxed" id="hl-sentence-en" data-en>&nbsp;</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-700 mt-2 leading-relaxed" id="hl-sentence-tl" data-tl>&nbsp;</p>
    </div>

    <p data-en class="mt-5 mb-3 text-sm">
      <strong>Read this carefully.</strong> Radar (Sentinel-1) sees standing water as smooth and dark, but it
      under-sees flooding between buildings in dense areas. So the observed inundation here is a lower bound, and it is
      cleanest in open, low-rise, and floodplain barangays. This page lines up flooding and canopy so they can be
      checked together. It does not claim trees cause or prevent a barangay flood.
    </p>
    <p data-tl class="mt-5 mb-3 text-sm">
      <strong>Basahin nang maigi.</strong> Nakikita ng radar (Sentinel-1) ang nakatayong tubig bilang makinis at madilim,
      ngunit hirap itong makita ang baha sa pagitan ng mga gusali sa siksik na lugar. Kaya ang nakitang baha dito ay
      pinakamababang tantiya, at pinakamalinaw sa mga bukas at mababang barangay. Pinagtatabi ng pahinang ito ang baha at
      canopy para masuri nang magkasama. Hindi nito sinasabing puno ang sanhi o lunas ng baha sa barangay.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── what actually predicts flooding (diverging bars from JSON) ────── -->
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>What actually predicts where it flooded</h2>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Ano ang humuhula kung saan bumaha</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-en>
      Each bar is one factor's standardized pull on observed inundation across the {""}
      <span id="nb-barangays">&mdash;</span> barangays, holding the others fixed. Bars left of the line push flooding
      down, bars right push it up. Canopy is the short one.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-tl>
      Bawat bar ay lakas ng isang salik sa nakitang baha sa {""}
      <span id="nb-barangays-tl">&mdash;</span> barangay, habang nakapirmi ang iba. Ang nasa kaliwa ng linya ay
      nagpapababa ng baha, ang nasa kanan ay nagtataas. Maikli ang sa canopy.
    </p>

    <div class="border border-ink-300/50 bg-paper p-4 sm:p-5">
      <div id="beta-bars" class="space-y-2.5"></div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-ink-300/40 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 bg-forest-700"></span><span data-en>tree canopy</span><span data-tl>puno</span></span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="inline-block w-3 h-3 bg-sepia-500/70"></span><span data-en>other factors</span><span data-tl>ibang salik</span></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fig-caption" id="beta-caption-en" data-en>&nbsp;</p>
    <p class="fig-caption" id="beta-caption-tl" data-tl>&nbsp;</p>

    <!-- ── the shrinkage line (key stats strip) ─────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-px bg-ink-300/40 border border-ink-300/40 mt-6 font-mono">
      <div class="bg-paper p-3">
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-en>canopy, raw</p>
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-tl>canopy, hilaw</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-900 tabular-nums" id="kpi-beta-raw">&mdash;</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-3">
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-en>canopy, controlled</p>
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-tl>canopy, kontrolado</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-900 tabular-nums" id="kpi-beta-ctrl">&mdash;</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-3">
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-en>model fit (R&sup2;)</p>
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-tl>akma (R&sup2;)</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-900 tabular-nums" id="kpi-r2">&mdash;</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-3">
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-en>barangays flooded</p>
        <p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500" data-tl>barangay binaha</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink-900 tabular-nums" id="kpi-flooded">&mdash;</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fig-caption" id="stats-caption-en" data-en>&nbsp;</p>
    <p class="fig-caption" id="stats-caption-tl" data-tl>&nbsp;</p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── map ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>Where the radar saw water</h2>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Saan nakakita ng tubig ang radar</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3" data-en>
      Each shape is one barangay, shaded by the share of its land the radar flagged as new standing water on
      2025-07-23. Outlined barangays are the priority set: flood-exposed and in the lowest canopy third. Tap any
      barangay for its figures.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3" data-tl>
      Bawat hugis ay isang barangay, kulay ayon sa bahagi ng lupa nitong natukoy ng radar bilang bagong nakatayong
      tubig noong 2025-07-23. Ang may guhit-hangganan ay ang priority: binaha at nasa pinakamababang ikatlo ng canopy.
      Pindutin ang alinmang barangay para sa datos.
    </p>

    <div class="relative w-full border border-ink-900" style="height: clamp(380px, 60vh, 560px);">
      <div id="fl-map" class="w-full h-full bg-paper-tint"></div>
      <div id="fl-map-loading" class="absolute inset-0 z-10 flex items-center justify-center bg-paper-tint/85 pointer-events-none transition-opacity duration-300">
        <span class="font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-ink-700">Loading the map&hellip;</span>
      </div>
      <!-- legend -->
      <div class="map-panel absolute bottom-2 left-2 z-20 !p-2.5">
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500 mb-1" data-en>share of barangay flooded</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-ink-500 mb-1" data-tl>bahaging binaha</p>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-ink-500">
          <span>0%</span>
          <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-24 border border-ink-300" style="background:linear-gradient(to right,#eef2f0,#c6dbef,#6baed6,#2171b5,#08306b)"></span>
          <span>3%+</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 font-mono text-[10px] text-ink-500 mt-1.5">
          <span class="inline-block h-2.5 w-5 border-2 border-umber-700"></span>
          <span data-en>priority barangay</span><span data-tl>priority na barangay</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="fig-caption" data-en>
      Inundation: Sentinel-1 SAR (COPERNICUS/S1_GRD) change detection, 2025-07-23 against a May to June dry reference.
      Permanent water and steep ground are excluded. A radar lower bound: dense built-up flooding is under-counted.
    </p>
    <p class="fig-caption" data-tl>
      Baha: Sentinel-1 SAR (COPERNICUS/S1_GRD) change detection, 2025-07-23 laban sa tuyong sanggunian noong Mayo hanggang
      Hunyo. Hindi kasama ang permanenteng tubig at matarik na lupa. Pinakamababang tantiya: kulang ang bilang sa siksik na lugar.
    </p>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── priority list ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>The priority screen</h2>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Ang priority na talaan</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-en>
      This is the honest, useful product: barangays that are both flood-exposed and tree-poor. Trees are not the flood
      lever here, but these are the places where drainage upgrades and urban forestry both make sense, and where a
      cutting permit deserves a closer look. A co-occurrence screen for prioritization, not a causal verdict.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-tl>
      Ito ang tapat at kapaki-pakinabang na produkto: mga barangay na binaha at kulang sa puno. Hindi puno ang lunas ng
      baha dito, ngunit dito may saysay ang pagpapaayos ng drainage at pagtatanim ng puno, at dito dapat suriing mabuti
      ang permiso sa pagputol. Talaan ng pagsasabay para sa pagbibigay-priyoridad, hindi hatol ng sanhi.
    </p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-5 px-5 sm:mx-0 sm:px-0">
    <table class="w-full text-sm border border-ink-300/40">
      <thead class="bg-paper-tint">
        <tr class="text-left font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-sepia-500">
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 w-8">#</th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30"><span data-en>barangay</span><span data-tl>barangay</span></th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 text-right"><span data-en>flooded %</span><span data-tl>binaha %</span></th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 text-right"><span data-en>canopy %</span><span data-tl>canopy %</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="fl-priority-tbody" class="font-mono tabular-nums text-[13px]"></tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-ink-500 mt-2" id="fl-priority-note">&nbsp;</p>

    <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>Most flood-exposed barangays</h3>
    <h3 class="font-display text-xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Pinaka-binahang barangay</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-en>
      The barangays where the radar saw the most water, regardless of canopy. Notice many are not tree-poor: open,
      low-lying ground is what the radar reads best, which is exactly why a raw canopy correlation misleads.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-4" data-tl>
      Ang mga barangay kung saan pinakamaraming tubig ang nakita ng radar, anuman ang canopy. Marami ang hindi kulang sa
      puno: bukas at mababang lupa ang pinakamadaling mabasa ng radar, kaya nga nakakalito ang hilaw na ugnayan ng canopy.
    </p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto -mx-5 px-5 sm:mx-0 sm:px-0">
    <table class="w-full text-sm border border-ink-300/40">
      <thead class="bg-paper-tint">
        <tr class="text-left font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.1em] text-sepia-500">
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 w-8">#</th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30"><span data-en>barangay</span><span data-tl>barangay</span></th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 text-right"><span data-en>flooded %</span><span data-tl>binaha %</span></th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 text-right"><span data-en>canopy %</span><span data-tl>canopy %</span></th>
          <th class="px-2 py-2 border-b border-ink-300/30 text-right"><span data-en>low ground</span><span data-tl>lapit-tubig</span></th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody id="fl-top-tbody" class="font-mono tabular-nums text-[13px]"></tbody>
    </table>
    </div>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── what it can / cannot say ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>What this can and cannot tell you</h2>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Ano ang masasabi at hindi masasabi nito</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-en>It can</p>
        <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-tl>Kaya nito</p>
        <ul data-en class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Show where radar saw standing water in one severe Metro Manila flood, by barangay.</li>
          <li>Test the canopy and flooding link properly, holding low ground, built-up share, and distance to water fixed.</li>
          <li>Flag barangays that are both flood-exposed and tree-poor, for combined drainage and urban-forestry action.</li>
          <li>Show that a raw canopy correlation runs backwards here, and why.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul data-tl class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Ipakita kung saan nakakita ng tubig ang radar sa isang malubhang baha sa Metro Manila, kada barangay.</li>
          <li>Subukin nang tama ang ugnayan ng canopy at baha, habang nakapirmi ang mababang lupa, gusali, at layo sa tubig.</li>
          <li>Tukuyin ang mga barangay na binaha at kulang sa puno, para sa sabayang drainage at pagtatanim.</li>
          <li>Ipakita na baligtad ang hilaw na ugnayan ng canopy dito, at kung bakit.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-en>It cannot</p>
        <p class="kicker text-ink-500 mb-2" data-tl>Hindi kaya nito</p>
        <ul data-en class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Say trees cause or prevent a barangay flood. This is an observed correlation, not an experiment.</li>
          <li>Catch every flood. Radar under-sees water inside dense built-up cores, so figures are a lower bound.</li>
          <li>Stand on one storm. It reads the July 2025 event, the most severe recent flood with clean radar.</li>
          <li>Resolve a single street. Below about 30 m, inundation is not independently visible.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul data-tl class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Sabihing puno ang sanhi o lunas ng baha. Ugnayan ito, hindi eksperimento.</li>
          <li>Mahuli ang bawat baha. Hirap makita ng radar ang tubig sa siksik na lugar, kaya pinakamababang tantiya.</li>
          <li>Umasa sa isang bagyo lamang. Binabasa nito ang baha ng Hulyo 2025, ang pinakamalubha kamakailan na may malinis na radar.</li>
          <li>Suriin ang isang kalye. Sa ilalim ng mga 30 m, hindi nakikita nang malinaw ang baha.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <!-- ── method + data + citation ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-en>Data and method</h2>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-ink-900 mt-8 mb-3" data-tl>Datos at paraan</h2>
    <p data-en class="text-sm mb-3">
      Observed inundation is Sentinel-1 radar change detection for 2025-07-23 against a dry May to June reference, with
      permanent water and steep ground removed. Confounders are height above nearest drainage and elevation (MERIT
      Hydro), built-up fraction (Dynamic World), and distance to water (JRC Global Surface Water). The model is a linear
      fit on standardized predictors with conservative error estimates, plus a logistic check and a test for spatial
      clustering in the residuals.
      Per-barangay figures: <a href="https://github.com/xmpuspus/leaves-ph/blob/main/data/flood/flood_canopy_barangay.csv" class={link}>flood_canopy_barangay.csv</a>.
      Map polygons: <a href="/data/flood_canopy_barangay.geojson" class={link}>flood_canopy_barangay.geojson</a>. Both
      regenerable with <code>make compute-flood</code>. CC-BY-4.0.
    </p>
    <p data-tl class="text-sm mb-3">
      Ang nakitang baha ay Sentinel-1 radar change detection para sa 2025-07-23 laban sa tuyong sanggunian noong Mayo
      hanggang Hunyo, walang permanenteng tubig at matarik na lupa. Ang mga confounder ay taas mula sa pinakamalapit na
      daluyan at elevation (MERIT Hydro), dami ng gusali (Dynamic World), at layo sa tubig (JRC Global Surface Water).
      Ang modelo ay matibay na linear fit sa standardized na salik, may logistic na pagsusuri at spatial na pagsusuri ng
      residuals. Datos kada barangay: <a href="https://github.com/xmpuspus/leaves-ph/blob/main/data/flood/flood_canopy_barangay.csv" class={link}>flood_canopy_barangay.csv</a>.
      Polygon ng mapa: <a href="/data/flood_canopy_barangay.geojson" class={link}>flood_canopy_barangay.geojson</a>.
      Mabubuo muli gamit ang <code>make compute-flood</code>. CC-BY-4.0.
    </p>
    <p data-en class="text-sm mb-3 text-ink-500">
      Official modeled flood-hazard layers (DOST GeoRiskPH, Project NOAH) would be a useful second lens, but their data
      is auth-gated or has no addressable download, so we measure inundation directly instead. Pairing the two is on the
      roadmap. The canopy model behind the rest of the site is on <a href="/methodology" class={link}>methodology</a>.
    </p>
    <p data-tl class="text-sm mb-3 text-ink-500">
      Magandang pangalawang lente ang opisyal na flood-hazard (DOST GeoRiskPH, Project NOAH), ngunit naka-auth-gate o
      walang ma-download na datos, kaya direktang sinusukat namin ang baha. Nasa roadmap ang pagsasama ng dalawa. Ang
      canopy model ng buong site ay nasa <a href="/methodology" class={link}>methodology</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="font-mono text-[11px] text-ink-500 mt-6" id="fl-disclaimer">&nbsp;</p>
  </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  #fl-root[data-lang="en"] [data-tl] { display: none !important; }
  #fl-root[data-lang="tl"] [data-en] { display: none !important; }
</style>

<script>
  import maplibregl from "maplibre-gl";
  import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";

  // ColorBrewer Blues ramp, matching the map legend. Self-contained so the page
  // does not depend on a d3 type export that is missing in the installed types.
  const FLOOD_RAMP = ["#eef2f0", "#c6dbef", "#6baed6", "#2171b5", "#08306b"];
  function hexLerp(a: string, b: string, t: number): string {
    const pa = [1, 3, 5].map((i) => parseInt(a.slice(i, i + 2), 16));
    const pb = [1, 3, 5].map((i) => parseInt(b.slice(i, i + 2), 16));
    const c = pa.map((v, i) => Math.round(v + (pb[i] - v) * t));
    return `rgb(${c[0]},${c[1]},${c[2]})`;
  }
  function rampColor(t: number): string {
    const x = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, t)) * (FLOOD_RAMP.length - 1);
    const i = Math.min(FLOOD_RAMP.length - 2, Math.floor(x));
    return hexLerp(FLOOD_RAMP[i], FLOOD_RAMP[i + 1], x - i);
  }

  type Props = Record<string, any>;
  type Reg = {
    ols_bivariate: { r2: number; coef: Record<string, number>; p: Record<string, number> };
    ols_controlled: { r2: number; coef: Record<string, number>; p: Record<string, number> };
    canopy_beta_bivariate: number;
    canopy_beta_controlled: number;
    vif: Record<string, number>;
    spatial_residual_moran: { I: number; p_sim: number; k: number } | null;
  };
  type Summary = {
    event: string;
    n_barangays: number;
    n_observed_inundation: number;
    n_priority: number;
    flood_pct_max: number;
    raw_canopy_flood_pearson_r: number;
    regression: Reg;
    top_flood_exposed: { barangay: string; lgu: string; flood_pct: number; canopy_pct: number; hand_m: number }[];
    priority_barangays: { barangay: string; lgu: string; flood_pct: number; canopy_pct: number; hand_m: number }[];
    disclaimer: string;
  };

  const root = document.getElementById("fl-root") as HTMLElement | null;
  const FLOOD_FULL = 3; // map colour saturates at 3% of a barangay flooded

  // friendly labels for the standardized predictors
  const LABELS: Record<string, { en: string; tl: string }> = {
    z_canopy_pct_2025: { en: "tree canopy", tl: "puno" },
    z_builtup_prob: { en: "built-up fraction", tl: "dami ng gusali" },
    z_hand_m: { en: "height above drainage", tl: "taas sa daluyan" },
    z_elev_m: { en: "elevation", tl: "elevation" },
    z_dist_water_m: { en: "distance to water", tl: "layo sa tubig" },
  };

  function curLang(): "en" | "tl" {
    return root?.dataset.lang === "tl" ? "tl" : "en";
  }
  function fmtSigned(n: number, d = 3): string {
    return (n >= 0 ? "+" : "") + n.toFixed(d);
  }
  function stars(p: number): string {
    return p < 0.001 ? "***" : p < 0.01 ? "**" : p < 0.05 ? "*" : "";
  }
  function colorForFlood(pct: number | null | undefined): string {
    if (pct == null || pct <= 0.01) return FLOOD_RAMP[0];
    return rampColor(pct / FLOOD_FULL);
  }

  // ── language toggle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  const btnEn = document.getElementById("lang-en");
  const btnTl = document.getElementById("lang-tl");
  function setLang(lang: "en" | "tl") {
    if (!root) return;
    root.dataset.lang = lang;
    const on = "bg-forest-700 text-paper";
    const off = "bg-paper text-ink-700";
    if (btnEn && btnTl) {
      btnEn.className = `px-2.5 py-1 ${lang === "en" ? on : off}`;
      btnTl.className = `px-2.5 py-1 ${lang === "tl" ? on : off}`;
      btnEn.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(lang === "en"));
      btnTl.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(lang === "tl"));
    }
    try { localStorage.setItem("fl_lang", lang); } catch {}
    renderDynamic();
  }
  btnEn?.addEventListener("click", () => setLang("en"));
  btnTl?.addEventListener("click", () => setLang("tl"));

  let summary: Summary | null = null;

  // ── headline verdict + sentence ──────────────────────────────────────
  function renderHeadline() {
    if (!summary) return;
    const tl = curLang() === "tl";
    const r = summary.regression;
    const bRaw = r.canopy_beta_bivariate;
    const bCtrl = r.canopy_beta_controlled;
    const pCtrl = r.ols_controlled.p["z_canopy_pct_2025"];
    const verdict = document.getElementById("hl-verdict");
    if (verdict) verdict.textContent = tl ? "Hindi ang puno." : "Not the trees.";
    const en = document.getElementById("hl-sentence-en");
    const tlEl = document.getElementById("hl-sentence-tl");
    if (en)
      en.textContent =
        `Across ${summary.n_barangays} Metro Manila barangays, the raw link runs backwards: greener barangays show more ` +
        `radar-detected flooding (r = ${fmtSigned(summary.raw_canopy_flood_pearson_r, 2)}), because radar under-sees water ` +
        `inside dense built-up cores. Control for low ground, built-up fraction, and distance to water, and canopy's own ` +
        `pull shrinks from ${fmtSigned(bRaw)} to ${fmtSigned(bCtrl)} and is no longer significant (p = ${pCtrl.toFixed(2)}). ` +
        `At this scale, flooding tracks low ground and how built-up a barangay is, not its tree cover.`;
    if (tlEl)
      tlEl.textContent =
        `Sa ${summary.n_barangays} barangay sa Metro Manila, baligtad ang hilaw na ugnayan: mas maraming natukoy na baha ng ` +
        `radar sa mas luntiang barangay (r = ${fmtSigned(summary.raw_canopy_flood_pearson_r, 2)}), dahil hirap makita ng radar ` +
        `ang tubig sa siksik na lugar. Kapag isinaalang-alang ang mababang lupa, dami ng gusali, at layo sa tubig, lumiliit ang ` +
        `lakas ng canopy mula ${fmtSigned(bRaw)} hanggang ${fmtSigned(bCtrl)} at hindi na makabuluhan (p = ${pCtrl.toFixed(2)}). ` +
        `Sa antas na ito, sumusunod ang baha sa mababang lupa at dami ng semento, hindi sa puno.`;
    const disc = document.getElementById("fl-disclaimer");
    if (disc) disc.textContent = summary.disclaimer;
  }

  // ── diverging beta bars ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  function renderBetas() {
    if (!summary) return;
    const tl = curLang() === "tl";
    const host = document.getElementById("beta-bars");
    if (!host) return;
    const coef = summary.regression.ols_controlled.coef;
    const pv = summary.regression.ols_controlled.p;
    const keys = Object.keys(LABELS).filter((k) => k in coef);
    const maxAbs = Math.max(...keys.map((k) => Math.abs(coef[k])), 0.02);
    const ordered = keys.slice().sort((a, b) => Math.abs(coef[b]) - Math.abs(coef[a]));
    host.innerHTML = ordered
      .map((k) => {
        const v = coef[k];
        const isCanopy = k === "z_canopy_pct_2025";
        const w = (Math.abs(v) / maxAbs) * 50; // half-width %
        const bar = `<span class="absolute top-0 bottom-0 ${isCanopy ? "bg-forest-700" : "bg-sepia-500/70"}"
          style="${v >= 0 ? `left:50%;width:${w}%` : `right:50%;width:${w}%`}"></span>`;
        return `<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-28 sm:w-40 shrink-0 text-[11px] sm:text-xs ${isCanopy ? "text-forest-700 font-semibold" : "text-ink-700"}">${LABELS[k][tl ? "tl" : "en"]}</span>
          <span class="relative flex-1 h-4 bg-paper-tint border-l border-ink-400">${bar}</span>
          <span class="w-14 shrink-0 text-right font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums ${isCanopy ? "text-forest-700" : "text-ink-700"}">${fmtSigned(v)}${stars(pv[k])}</span>
        </div>`;
      })
      .join("");

    const nb = document.getElementById("nb-barangays");
    const nbtl = document.getElementById("nb-barangays-tl");
    if (nb) nb.textContent = String(summary.n_barangays);
    if (nbtl) nbtl.textContent = String(summary.n_barangays);

    const capEn = document.getElementById("beta-caption-en");
    const capTl = document.getElementById("beta-caption-tl");
    if (capEn)
      capEn.textContent =
        "Standardized coefficients from the controlled linear model. Stars mark significance (* p<0.05, ** p<0.01, *** p<0.001). " +
        "Built-up's strong negative pull is largely a radar detection effect (water is hidden between buildings), plus real drainage. " +
        "Canopy's bar is short and not significant.";
    if (capTl)
      capTl.textContent =
        "Standardized na coefficient mula sa matibay na linear model. Ang bituin ay tanda ng kahalagahan (* p<0.05, ** p<0.01, *** p<0.001). " +
        "Ang malakas na negatibong lakas ng gusali ay higit na epekto ng radar (tinatago ang tubig sa pagitan ng gusali), kasama ang totoong drainage. " +
        "Maikli at hindi makabuluhan ang bar ng canopy.";
  }

  // ── stats strip ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  function renderStats() {
    if (!summary) return;
    const r = summary.regression;
    const set = (id: string, v: string) => {
      const el = document.getElementById(id);
      if (el) el.textContent = v;
    };
    set("kpi-beta-raw", fmtSigned(r.canopy_beta_bivariate));
    set("kpi-beta-ctrl", fmtSigned(r.canopy_beta_controlled));
    set("kpi-r2", `${r.ols_bivariate.r2.toFixed(2)}→${r.ols_controlled.r2.toFixed(2)}`);
    set("kpi-flooded", `${summary.n_observed_inundation}/${summary.n_barangays}`);

    const moran = r.spatial_residual_moran;
    const capEn = document.getElementById("stats-caption-en");
    const capTl = document.getElementById("stats-caption-tl");
    const moranEn = moran
      ? ` Residuals show weak but real spatial clustering (Moran's I ${fmtSigned(moran.I, 2)}, p ${moran.p_sim.toFixed(3)}), so standard errors are read conservatively.`
      : "";
    const moranTl = moran
      ? ` May mahina ngunit totoong spatial clustering ang residuals (Moran's I ${fmtSigned(moran.I, 2)}, p ${moran.p_sim.toFixed(3)}).`
      : "";
    if (capEn)
      capEn.textContent =
        `Canopy's standardized pull more than halves once the real flood drivers are added, and the model explains far ` +
        `more of where it flooded. ${summary.n_priority} barangays are both flood-exposed and in the lowest canopy third.` +
        moranEn;
    if (capTl)
      capTl.textContent =
        `Lumiliit nang higit sa kalahati ang lakas ng canopy kapag idinagdag ang tunay na sanhi ng baha, at mas naipapaliwanag ` +
        `ng modelo kung saan bumaha. ${summary.n_priority} barangay ang binaha at nasa pinakamababang ikatlo ng canopy.` +
        moranTl;
  }

  // ── tables ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  function row(i: number, r: Props, withGround: boolean): string {
    const ground = withGround
      ? `<td class="px-2 py-1.5 text-right text-ink-500">${Number(r.hand_m).toFixed(1)} m</td>`
      : "";
    return `<tr class="border-t border-ink-300/40 hover:bg-paper-tint/60 cursor-pointer" data-brgy="${String(r.barangay)}" data-lgu="${String(r.lgu)}">
      <td class="px-2 py-1.5 text-ink-500">${i + 1}</td>
      <td class="px-2 py-1.5"><span class="text-ink-900">${String(r.barangay)}</span><span class="block text-[10px] text-sepia-500 uppercase tracking-[0.06em]">${String(r.lgu)}</span></td>
      <td class="px-2 py-1.5 text-right text-ink-900">${Number(r.flood_pct).toFixed(2)}%</td>
      <td class="px-2 py-1.5 text-right text-ink-900">${Number(r.canopy_pct).toFixed(1)}%</td>
      ${ground}
    </tr>`;
  }
  function wireRows(tbody: HTMLElement) {
    tbody.querySelectorAll("tr[data-brgy]").forEach((tr) => {
      tr.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const b = (tr as HTMLElement).dataset.brgy;
        const l = (tr as HTMLElement).dataset.lgu;
        const f = features.find(
          (g) => g.properties.barangay_name === b && g.properties.lgu_name === l,
        );
        if (f && map) flyToFeature(f);
      });
    });
  }
  function renderTables() {
    if (!summary) return;
    const pri = document.getElementById("fl-priority-tbody");
    if (pri) {
      pri.innerHTML = summary.priority_barangays.map((r, i) => row(i, r, false)).join("");
      wireRows(pri);
    }
    const top = document.getElementById("fl-top-tbody");
    if (top) {
      top.innerHTML = summary.top_flood_exposed.map((r, i) => row(i, r, true)).join("");
      wireRows(top);
    }
    const note = document.getElementById("fl-priority-note");
    if (note)
      note.textContent =
        curLang() === "tl"
          ? `${summary.n_priority} barangay na binaha at kulang sa puno. Pindutin ang hilera para sa mapa.`
          : `${summary.n_priority} barangays both flood-exposed and tree-poor. Tap a row to find it on the map.`;
  }

  function renderDynamic() {
    renderHeadline();
    renderBetas();
    renderStats();
    renderTables();
  }

  // ── map ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  let map: any = null;
  let features: any[] = [];
  let popup: any = null;

  function popupHTML(p: Props): string {
    const tl = curLang() === "tl";
    const floodLbl = tl ? "ng barangay na binaha" : "of barangay flooded";
    const canopyLbl = tl ? "canopy" : "tree canopy";
    const handLbl = tl ? "taas sa daluyan" : "height above drainage";
    return `<div style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;line-height:1.55;color:#1a1a1a;padding:9px 11px;max-width:240px;">
      <div style="font-family:'PT Serif',serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.2;">${String(p.barangay_name || "")}</div>
      <div style="color:#5a4f3a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;font-size:10px;margin-top:2px;">${String(p.lgu_name || "")}</div>
      <div style="margin-top:7px;color:#08519c;">${Number(p.flood_pct).toFixed(2)}% ${floodLbl}</div>
      <div>${Number(p.canopy_pct).toFixed(1)}% ${canopyLbl}</div>
      <div style="color:#5a4f3a;">${handLbl}: ${Number(p.hand_m).toFixed(1)} m</div>
      ${Number(p.priority) === 1 ? `<div style="color:#8b3f1d;margin-top:4px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;font-size:10px;">${tl ? "priority na barangay" : "priority barangay"}</div>` : ""}
    </div>`;
  }
  function flyToFeature(f: any) {
    if (!map) return;
    const c = featureCenter(f);
    if (!c) return;
    map.flyTo({ center: c, zoom: 12.5, speed: 1.2 });
    if (popup) popup.remove();
    popup = new maplibregl.Popup({ maxWidth: "260px", closeButton: true })
      .setLngLat(c)
      .setHTML(popupHTML(f.properties))
      .addTo(map);
  }
  function featureCenter(f: any): [number, number] | null {
    // crude centroid from the first ring; good enough to fly to
    const g = f.geometry;
    let ring: number[][] | null = null;
    if (g.type === "Polygon") ring = g.coordinates[0];
    else if (g.type === "MultiPolygon") ring = g.coordinates[0][0];
    if (!ring || !ring.length) return null;
    let x = 0, y = 0;
    for (const pt of ring) { x += pt[0]; y += pt[1]; }
    return [x / ring.length, y / ring.length];
  }

  async function init() {
    const [sumRes, gjRes] = await Promise.all([
      fetch("/data/flood_canopy_summary.json"),
      fetch("/data/flood_canopy_barangay.geojson"),
    ]);
    summary = (await sumRes.json()) as Summary;
    const gj = await gjRes.json();
    features = gj.features || [];
    for (const f of features) f.properties._fill = colorForFlood(f.properties.flood_pct);

    renderDynamic();

    map = new maplibregl.Map({
      container: "fl-map",
      style: {
        version: 8,
        sources: {
          osm: {
            type: "raster",
            tiles: [
              "https://a.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png",
              "https://b.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png",
              "https://c.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png",
            ],
            tileSize: 256,
            attribution: "&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors",
          },
        },
        layers: [
          { id: "osm", type: "raster", source: "osm", paint: { "raster-saturation": -0.5, "raster-opacity": 0.55 } },
        ],
      },
      center: [121.02, 14.6],
      zoom: 10.2,
      maxZoom: 15,
      minZoom: 9,
      attributionControl: { compact: true },
    });
    map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }), "top-right");
    map.fitBounds([[120.9, 14.4], [121.15, 14.78]], { padding: 18, animate: false });

    map.on("load", () => {
      map.addSource("fl", { type: "geojson", data: gj });
      map.addLayer({
        id: "fl-fill",
        type: "fill",
        source: "fl",
        paint: { "fill-color": ["get", "_fill"], "fill-opacity": 0.82 },
      });
      map.addLayer({
        id: "fl-outline",
        type: "line",
        source: "fl",
        paint: { "line-color": "#1a1a1a", "line-width": 0.3, "line-opacity": 0.4 },
      });
      map.addLayer({
        id: "fl-priority",
        type: "line",
        source: "fl",
        filter: ["==", ["get", "priority"], 1],
        paint: { "line-color": "#b8431f", "line-width": 2, "line-opacity": 0.95 },
      });
      map.on("click", "fl-fill", (e: any) => {
        const f = e.features?.[0];
        if (!f) return;
        if (popup) popup.remove();
        popup = new maplibregl.Popup({ maxWidth: "260px", closeButton: true })
          .setLngLat(e.lngLat)
          .setHTML(popupHTML(f.properties))
          .addTo(map);
      });
      map.on("mouseenter", "fl-fill", () => (map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer"));
      map.on("mouseleave", "fl-fill", () => (map.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""));
      const load = document.getElementById("fl-map-loading");
      if (load) {
        load.style.opacity = "0";
        window.setTimeout(() => (load.style.display = "none"), 320);
      }
    });
  }

  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem("fl_lang");
    if (saved === "tl") setLang("tl");
  } catch {}

  init().catch((err) => {
    console.error("flood-risk init failed", err);
    const load = document.getElementById("fl-map-loading");
    if (load) load.innerHTML = '<span class="font-mono text-[12px] text-umber-700">Data failed to load. Retry shortly.</span>';
  });
</script>
